# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is deliberately tracked, not ignored. `fireup` ships a binary, and
# Cargo's guidance is to commit the lock file for binaries so that a build of a
# given commit resolves the same dependency versions every time. CI asserts the
# lock file stays in step with Cargo.toml by passing `--locked`.

